[{"location":"guides/getting-started/#getting-started","page":"Getting Started","title":"Getting Started","text":"In this tutorial, we introduduce the basics of using SolarDiodeModels.jl.","category":"section"},{"location":"contributing/#contributing","page":"Contributing guidelines","title":"Contributing guidelines","text":"First of all, thanks for the interest!\n\nWe welcome all kinds of contribution, including, but not limited to code, documentation, examples, configuration, issue creating, etc.\n\nBe polite and respectful.","category":"section"},{"location":"contributing/#Bug-reports-and-discussions","page":"Contributing guidelines","title":"Bug reports and discussions","text":"If you think you found a bug, feel free to open an issue.\n\nFocused suggestions and requests can also be opened as issues.\n\ninfo: Info\nBefore opening a pull request, it can be productive to first start an issue or a discussion on the topic so that the maintainers and community can provide feedback.","category":"section"},{"location":"contributing/#Working-on-an-issue","page":"Contributing guidelines","title":"Working on an issue","text":"If you found an issue that interests you, comment on that issue what your plans are. If the solution to the issue is clear, you can immediately create a pull request (see below ). Otherwise, say what your proposed solution is and wait for a discussion around it.\n\ntip: Tip\nFeel free to ping us after a few days if there are no responses.","category":"section"},{"location":"reference/#reference","page":"API reference","title":"API reference","text":"This page provides comprehensive documentation for all functions and types in SolarDiodeModels.jl.","category":"section"},{"location":"reference/#Contents","page":"API reference","title":"Contents","text":"Pages = [\"reference.md\"]","category":"section"},{"location":"reference/#Index","page":"API reference","title":"Index","text":"Pages = [\"reference.md\"]","category":"section"},{"location":"reference/#Diode-Models","page":"API reference","title":"Diode Models","text":"The following diode models are implemented in SolarDiodeModels.jl:","category":"section"},{"location":"reference/#SolarDiodeModels.DiodeModels.PVsyst","page":"API reference","title":"SolarDiodeModels.DiodeModels.PVsyst","text":"PVsyst\n\nA struct representing the PVsyst [SRH14] diode model.\n\nFields\n\nConstructor\n\nPVsyst(): Creates a new instance of the DeSoto diode model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"reference/#SolarDiodeModels.DiodeModels.DeSoto","page":"API reference","title":"SolarDiodeModels.DiodeModels.DeSoto","text":"DeSoto\n\nA struct representing the DeSoto diode model.\n\nFields\n\nConstructor\n\nDeSoto(): Creates a new instance of the DeSoto diode model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"#Home","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"#SolarDiodeModels.jl","page":"Home","title":"SolarDiodeModels.jl","text":"(Image: Stable) (Image: Development documentation)\n\n(Image: Test workflow status) (Image: Coverage) (Image: Lint workflow Status) (Image: Docs workflow Status) (Image: Aqua QA) (Image: tested with JET.jl)\n\nSolarDiodeModels.jl implements basic single diode solar cell and module models in Julia. It is part of the JuliaSolarPV organization.","category":"section"},{"location":"#Example-Usage","page":"Home","title":"Example Usage","text":"julia> using SolarDiodeModels\n","category":"section"},{"location":"#How-to-Cite","page":"Home","title":"How to Cite","text":"If you use SolarDiodeModels.jl in your work, please cite using the reference given in CITATION.cff.","category":"section"},{"location":"#Contributing","page":"Home","title":"Contributing","text":"If you want to make contributions of any kind, please first take a look at our contributing guide directly on GitHub or the contributing page on the website","category":"section"},{"location":"literature/#Literature","page":"Literature","title":"Literature","text":"K. J. Sauer, T. Roessler and C. W. Hansen. Modeling the irradiance and temperature dependence of photovoltaic modules in PVsyst. IEEE Journal of Photovoltaics 5, 152–158 (2014).\n\n\n\n","category":"section"}]
